{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Voice.</b> The nature of the mountain is that when a person speaks to echo back the voice, and this is the sense of קול המון, from the root הומה (1 Kings 1:41). Now he explained why this is קול השאון [voice of tumult] among kingdoms of nations, for the king of Persia, who is Cyrus, and the king of Media, who is Darius — both of them joined against Babylon, and this is explicit in the book of Daniel (Daniel 5:28)." "<b>Appoints.</b> He sets officers or commanders, and it is a verb taking two objects."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The printed text reads שאון; Ibn Ezra's argument requires קול השאון, as noted by the standard correction [צ\"ל]."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:34.813970979Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}